ELEMENTARY TRANSCENDENTAL FUNCTIONS (p.78)
4.3.131  \sin(x+iy)=\sin x\cosh y+i\cos x\sinh y
4.3.132  \cos(x+iy)=\cos x\cosh y-i\sin x\sinh y
4.3.133  \tan(x+iy)=\frac{\sin2x+i\sinh2y}{\cos2x+\cosh2y}
4.3.134  |\sin(x+iy)|^2=\sin^2x+\sinh^2y
4.3.135  |\cos(x+iy)|^2=\cos^2x+\sinh^2y
4.3.136  |\tan(x+iy)|^2=\frac{\sin^2x+\sinh^2y}{\cos^2x+\sinh^2y}
Right Triangle: sides a, b, hypotenuse c, angle A opposite a, angle B opposite b, C=90^\circ
4.3.137  a=c\sin A=c\cos B=b\tan A
4.3.138  b=c\sin B=c\cos A=a\tan B
4.3.139  c=\sqrt{a^2+b^2}
4.3.140  A+B=90^\circ
Oblique Triangle: sides a, b, c opposite angles A, B, C respectively
4.3.141  A+B+C=180^\circ
4.3.142  \frac{a}{\sin A}=\frac{b}{\sin B}=\frac{c}{\sin C}\ \ \mathrm{(Law\ of\ Sines)}
4.3.143  c^2=a^2+b^2-2ab\cos C\ \ \mathrm{(Law\ of\ Cosines)}
4.3.144  a=b\cos C+c\cos B\ \ \mathrm{(Law\ of\ Tangents\ related\ form)}
4.3.145  \tan\tfrac12(A-B)=\frac{a-b}{a+b}\cot\tfrac12C
4.3.146  \mathrm{Area}=\tfrac12ab\sin C=\sqrt{s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)},\ s=\tfrac12(a+b+c)\ \ \mathrm{(Heron's\ formula)}
4.3.147  r=\frac{\mathrm{Area}}{s}\ \mathrm{(inradius)},\ R=\frac{abc}{4\,\mathrm{Area}}\ \mathrm{(circumradius)}
